oth parties observing  them at all times and so when  Republicans broke that bargain in 2016  they sort of they opened up a Pandora's  box of responses and so I think the  Democrats will be well within their  rights to add two justices to the  Supreme Court and the next time they're  in power I do think that they should  offer a truce to Republicans in the form  of a constitutional amendment and this  is what I actually think they should be  talking about right now is the way that  the process is unfair you know some  presidents get zero appointments in four  years Pat Carter got zero now Donald  Trump gets two in two years which is  it's just preposterous right and if we  have an amendment that capped tenure on  the court at 18 years gave every  president the right to appoint two  justices for every four-year term we  could could we could like take this  ugliness right out of our politics I  think Republicans will say no to that  and I've been I think that Democrats  have every right to pack the courts in  response let's talk a little bit about  the electoral college there has been  particularly after Donald Trump lost in  the popular vote to Hillary Clinton by  almost three million votes in 2016 a  renewed sort of call for eliminating the  electoral college in favor of like a  national popular vote and I'm curious  where where you kind of come down on it  from is it actually good strategy for  the left because on the one hand it  appears as though it has screwed  Democrats twice in the last five  elections but at the same time what  Trump said is true in the sense that if  you know going in that it's a popular  vote election and not an electoral  college election you do campaign  differently and I wonder if it's  actually that clear that it would be  good for Democrats to get rid of the  electoral college sure I mean it's a  good question I mean I think one thing  to keep in mind is that we almost did  have this situation in the opposite  direction in 2004 so if J